From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nullptr-t-oss <127822226+nullptr-t-oss@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Oct 2026 09:18:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ABI: use ABI padding for SYSVIPC

This commit allows us to enable CONFIG_SYSVIPC in defconfig without breaking kernel ABI.

Root cause: enabling CONFIG_SYSVIPC normally injects `struct sysv_sem` / `struct sysv_shm`
into the *middle* of task_struct, shifting every field that follows it. Vendor modules are
built against the frozen GKI ABI, so they would read the wrong offsets and the device
would bootloop. The fix moves those two fields onto the pre-existing ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE
(6/7/8) u64 padding slots, which ANDROID_KABI_USE() overlays as a union:

  - CONFIG_ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE=y (default y, drivers/android/Kconfig) makes the three
    padding slots real `u64 android_kabi_reserved6/7/8` members, so total task_struct
    size and all following offsets are unchanged.
  - _ANDROID_KABI_REPLACE() emits a _Static_assert that sizeof(sysv_sem) <= 8 and that
    alignment matches, so an overflow is a compile-time error, not a runtime bootloop.
  - ANDROID_KABI_USE() is *not* gated on CONFIG_ANDROID_KABI, only the RESERVE side is --
    which is why this works on a GKI tree that does not enforce kABI itself.
  - The __GENKSYMS__ path keeps the original reserve fields, so genksyms still sees the
    stable ABI.

Regenerated for THIS tree (seventeen @ 6.6.142) with exact context: `patch -p1` applies
it with no offset and no fuzz. Hunk line numbers moved from the 6.6.82 variant by +1
(site 1) and +6 (site 2), but the surrounding code is byte-identical, so the change is a
pure rebase.

Note this tree ALSO has CONFIG_GKI_DYNAMIC_TASK_STRUCT_SIZE=y (with
GKI_TASK_STRUCT_VENDOR_SIZE_MAX=1024). That is a different mechanism and does not
interact with this patch: it allocates the vendor area *after* sizeof(struct task_struct)
(include/linux/sched/task.h, `p + 1`), so it cannot shift any field inside the struct.
ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE still operates on slots inside task_struct.

The 6.6.82 variant of this patch lives in the kernel_xiaomi_sm8735 repository.

Signed-off-by: nullptr-t-oss <127822226+nullptr-t-oss@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 include/linux/sched.h | 14 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/include/linux/sched.h
+++ b/include/linux/sched.h
@@ -1076,8 +1076,8 @@
 	struct nameidata		*nameidata;

 #ifdef CONFIG_SYSVIPC
-	struct sysv_sem			sysvsem;
-	struct sysv_shm			sysvshm;
+	// struct sysv_sem			sysvsem;
+	// struct sysv_shm			sysvshm;
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_DETECT_HUNG_TASK
 	unsigned long			last_switch_count;
@@ -1530,9 +1530,15 @@
 	ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(3);
 	ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(4);
 	ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(5);
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_SYSVIPC
+	ANDROID_KABI_USE(6, struct sysv_sem sysvsem);
+	_ANDROID_KABI_REPLACE(ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(7); ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(8), struct sysv_shm sysvshm);
+#else
 	ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(6);
 	ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(7);
 	ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(8);
+#endif

 #ifdef CONFIG_RV
 	/*
